# header only, no other file; after 0001-0205). Owner 2026-11-21: after Play the game takes about 10 s to open. The start reads
# chaos.pack (about 0.9 GB: Tibia.dat / Tibia.spr shards, modules, data), GCM-decrypts it and inflates it into one buffer before
# any window exists, and 0102 did the three steps one chunk after the other: read + decrypt + inflate. Now one thread reads and
# decrypts a chunk ahead (a ring of four 4 MB chunks), the calling thread inflates: the start takes the longer of the two, not
# their sum. Measured (client/tools/chaospack_test.cpp builds it; a 200 MB sprite-like ZIP, 58 MB pack, one core each): with a
# disk of 120 MB/s 1.32 s -> 0.70 s, of 400 MB/s 0.88 s -> 0.74 s, from memory 0.72 s -> 0.75 s (nothing to overlap). Nothing else
# changes: same format, same checks (the tag, the exact end of the zlib stream, the exact length, `out` wiped on any failure),
# same signature; a pack of one chunk and a system that cannot make a thread run the old order on the calling thread. `read` is
# called from the second thread only (after the header), always in order. The test adds a 40 MB pack (ten chunks, more than the
# ring), an I/O error in the middle, an unreadable tag and a corrupt first / last chunk, and runs clean under ThreadSanitizer and
# AddressSanitizer. The build links pthread (the engine already does).
